{\rtf1\ansi\uc1{\*\generator WTS5;}\adeflang1025\adeff0\deff0\stshfdbch0\stshfloch0\stshfhich0\deflang1033\deflangfe1033{\fonttbl{\f0\fcharset0 Times New Roman;}{\f1\fcharset0 Latha;}{\f2\fcharset0 Arial;}{\f3\fcharset0 MEPS Bookman WTS;}{\f4\fbidi\fcharset177 Arial;}}{\colortbl ;\red128\green0\blue128;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;\red153\green204\blue0;\red102\green102\blue153;\red51\green51\blue204;\red153\green51\blue102;\red128\green0\blue0;}{\stylesheet {\s2\ltrpar\qc \rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f0\fs36\cf1\b \sbasedon0\snext21 Title;}{\s10\ltrpar\qc \rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\fs24\cf8\b \sbasedon0\snext25 Heading 1;}}\plain\langnp1033\langfenp1033\ltrdoc\fcs1\af0\afs24\acf0\fcs0\f0\fs24\cf0{\info\uc1{\upr{\*\ud{\author \u67?\u111?\u112?\u121?\u114?\u105?\u103?\u104?\u116?\u32?\u169?\u32?\u50?\u48?\u50?\u49?\u32?\u87?\u97?\u116?\u99?\u104?\u32?\u84?\u111?\u119?\u101?\u114?\u32?\u66?\u105?\u98?\u108?\u101?\u32?\u97?\u110?\u100?\u32?\u84?\u114?\u97?\u99?\u116?\u32?\u83?\u111?\u99?\u105?\u101?\u116?\u121?\u32?\u111?\u102?\u32?\u80?\u101?\u110?\u110?\u115?\u121?\u108?\u118?\u97?\u110?\u105?\u97?}}}{\upr{\*\ud{\title \u76?\u101?\u115?\u115?\u111?\u110?\u160?\u51?\u53?\u8212?\u72?\u111?\u119?\u32?\u116?\u111?\u32?\u77?\u97?\u107?\u101?\u32?\u71?\u111?\u111?\u100?\u32?\u68?\u101?\u99?\u105?\u115?\u105?\u111?\u110?\u115?}}}}\pard\plain\langnp1033\langfenp1033 \ltrpar\s2\qc {\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f0\fs36\cf1\b Lesson\u160?35\u8212?How to Make Good Decisions\par}\pard\plain\langnp1033\langfenp1033 \ltrpar\ql\fi576 {\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2 We all have decisions to make. Many of these decisions can have a big impact on us and our friendship with Jehovah. For example, we may have to decide where to live, how to support ourselves financially, or whether to get married. When we make good decisions, we can have a happy life and please Jehovah.\par}\pard\plain\langnp1033\langfenp1033 \ltrpar\ql\li720 {\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\cf2 [Image:]\u160?A husband researching cars advertised on a website as his wife and children look on.\par}\pard\plain\langnp1033\langfenp1033 \ltrpar\ql\fi576 {\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\b 1. How can you use the Bible to help you make good decisions?\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2 Before making a decision, pray for Jehovah\u8217?s help and examine the Bible to see how he views the matter. (Read Proverbs 2:3-6.) In some cases, Jehovah provides a clear command. If so, deciding to obey that command is the best choice you could make.\par}\pard\plain\langnp1033\langfenp1033 \ltrpar\ql\li720 {\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af2\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\cf2 [\u8220?Read\u8221? scripture] Proverbs 2:3-6: Moreover, if you call out for understanding And raise your voice for discernment; If you keep seeking for it as for silver, And you keep searching for it as for hidden treasures; Then you will understand the fear of Jehovah, And you will find the knowledge of God. For Jehovah himself gives wisdom; From his mouth come knowledge and discernment. [End of \u8220?Read\u8221? scripture]\par}\pard\plain\langnp1033\langfenp1033 \ltrpar\ql\fi576 {\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2 What, though, if there is no clear Bible command telling you what to do? Jehovah will still guide you }{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ab\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\b \u8220?in the way you should walk.\u8221? }{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2 (}{\field{\*\fldinst {HYPERLINK "https://www.jw.org/finder?pub=nwtsty&bible=23048017&wtlocale=E&srcid=share" }}{\fldrslt{\cs4\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\cf3\ul Isaiah 48:17}}}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2 ) How? There may be principles that can guide you. Bible principles are basic truths that reveal God\u8217?s thoughts and feelings. Often we learn how God feels about a matter when we read an account in the Bible. When we discern how Jehovah feels, we can make decisions that please him.\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ab\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\b 2. What factors should you consider before making a decision?\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2 The Bible says: }{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ab\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\b \u8220?The shrewd one ponders each step.\u8221? }{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2 (}{\field{\*\fldinst {HYPERLINK "https://www.jw.org/finder?pub=nwtsty&bible=20014015&wtlocale=E&srcid=share" }}{\fldrslt{\cs4\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\cf3\ul Proverbs 14:15}}}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2 ) This means that before we make a decision, we should take the time to think about our choices. As you evaluate each option, ask yourself: \u8216?What Bible principles apply? Which option will give me peace of mind? How will my decision affect others? Most important, will it make Jehovah happy?\u8217?\u8212?}{\field{\*\fldinst {HYPERLINK "https://www.jw.org/finder?pub=nwtsty&bible=05032029&wtlocale=E&srcid=share" }}{\fldrslt{\cs4\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\cf3\ul Deuteronomy 32:29}}}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2 .\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2 Jehovah has the right to tell us what is good and what is bad. When we get acquainted with his laws and principles and are determined to follow them, we are developing a good conscience. The conscience is our inner sense of right and wrong. (}{\field{\*\fldinst {HYPERLINK "https://www.jw.org/finder?pub=nwtsty&bible=45002014-45002015&wtlocale=E&srcid=share" }}{\fldrslt{\cs4\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\cf3\ul Romans 2:14,15}}}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2 ) A trained conscience will help us make good decisions.\par}\par\pard\plain\langnp1033\langfenp1033 \ltrpar\qc\fi576 {\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\cf3 Dig Deeper\par}\pard\plain\langnp1033\langfenp1033 \ltrpar\ql\fi576 {\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2 Take a closer look at how Bible principles and the conscience play important roles in decision-making.\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\b 3. Let the Bible guide you\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2 How can Bible principles guide us when making decisions? Play the video }{\field{\*\fldinst {HYPERLINK "https://www.jw.org/finder?srcid=share&wtlocale=E&lank=pub-lffv_356_VIDEO" }}{\fldrslt{\cs4\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\cf3\i\ul Let Bible Principles Guide You}}}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2  (5:54), and then discuss the questions that follow.\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2 \u8226? What is free will?\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2 \u8226? Why did Jehovah give us free will?\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2 \u8226? What has he provided to help us use our free will in the best way possible?\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2 To see an example of a Bible principle, }{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\b read }{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\cf2\b Ephesians 5:15, 1}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\b 6.}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2  Then discuss how you could make \u8220?the best use of your time\u8221? to\u160?...\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2 \u8226? read the Bible regularly.\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2 \u8226? become a better marriage mate, parent, son, or daughter.\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2 \u8226? attend congregation meetings.\par}\pard\plain\langnp1033\langfenp1033 \ltrpar\ql\li720 {\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af2\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\cf2 [\u8220?Read\u8221? scripture] Ephesians 5:15, 16: So keep strict watch that how you walk is not as unwise but as wise persons, making the best use of your time, because the days are wicked. [End of \u8220?Read\u8221? scripture]\par}\pard\plain\langnp1033\langfenp1033 \ltrpar\ql\fi576 {\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\b 4. Train your conscience to make good decisions\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2 When there is a clear Scriptural command about a matter, the right choice may seem easy. But what if there is no such command? Play the video }{\field{\*\fldinst {HYPERLINK "https://www.jw.org/finder?srcid=jwlshare&wtlocale=E&lank=pub-jwb_201807_3_VIDEO" }}{\fldrslt{\cs4\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\cf3\i\ul \u8220?Maintain a Good Conscience\u8221?}}}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2  (5:13), and then discuss the question that follows.\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2 \u8226? In the video, what steps did the sister take to train her conscience and to make a decision that would please Jehovah?\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2 Why should we not ask others to make decisions that we should make? }{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\b Read Hebrews 5:14, }{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2 and then discuss these questions:\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2 \u8226? While it may seem easier to ask others to make decisions for us, what should we be able to distinguish for ourselves?\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2 \u8226? What is available that can help you develop your conscience and make good decisions?\par}\pard\plain\langnp1033\langfenp1033 \ltrpar\ql\li720 {\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af2\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\cf2 [\u8220?Read\u8221? scripture] Hebrews 5:14: But solid food belongs to mature people, to those who through use have their powers of discernment trained to distinguish both right and wrong. [End of \u8220?Read\u8221? scripture]\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\cf2 Page\u160?148 [Image:]\u160?A person driving a car on a road. A GPS mounted on the dashboard helps the driver stay on the correct route.\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\cf2 Caption: Like a map, our conscience helps us decide where to go in life\par}\pard\plain\langnp1033\langfenp1033 \ltrpar\ql\fi576 {\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ab\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\cf2\b 5}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ab\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\b . Respect the consciences of others\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2 Different people will make different decisions. How can we show respect for the consciences of others? Consider two situations:\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ab\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\b Situation\u160?1: }{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2 A sister who likes to wear makeup moves to a congregation where many sisters are bothered when they see others wearing it.\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ab\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\b Read Romans 15:1 and }{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ab\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\cf2\b 1\u160?Corinthians 10:23, 2}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ab\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\b 4, }{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2 and then discuss these questions:\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2 \u8226? Based on these verses, what might that sister decide? What will you do if you are with a person whose conscience forbids doing something that your conscience allows you to do?\par}\pard\plain\langnp1033\langfenp1033 \ltrpar\ql\li720 {\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af2\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\cf2 [\u8220?Read\u8221? scriptures] Romans 15:1: We, though, who are strong ought to bear the weaknesses of those not strong, and not to be pleasing ourselves.\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af2\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\cf2 1 Corinthians 10:23, 24: All things are lawful, but not all things are advantageous. All things are lawful, but not all things build up. Let each one keep seeking, not his own advantage, but that of the other person. [End of \u8220?Read\u8221? scriptures]\par}\pard\plain\langnp1033\langfenp1033 \ltrpar\ql\fi576 {\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ab\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\b Situation\u160?2: }{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2 A brother knows that the Bible does not condemn using alcohol in moderation, but he chooses to abstain from it. He is invited to a social gathering where he sees brothers drinking alcohol.\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ab\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\b Read Ecclesiastes 7:16 and }{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ab\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\cf2\b Romans 14:1, 1}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ab\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\b 0, }{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2 and then discuss these questions:\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2 \u8226? Based on these verses, what might that brother decide? What will you do if you see another person doing something that your conscience keeps you from doing?\par}\pard\plain\langnp1033\langfenp1033 \ltrpar\ql\li720 {\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af2\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\cf2 [\u8220?Read\u8221? scriptures] Ecclesiastes 7:16: Do not be overly righteous, nor show yourself excessively wise. Why should you bring ruin to yourself?\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af2\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\cf2 Romans 14:1: Welcome the man having weaknesses in his faith, but do not pass judgment on differing opinions.\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af2\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\cf2 Romans 14:10: But why do you judge your brother? Or why do you also look down on your brother? For we will all stand before the judgment seat of God. [End of \u8220?Read\u8221? scriptures]\par}\pard\plain\langnp1033\langfenp1033 \ltrpar\ql\fi576 \par\pard\plain\langnp1033\langfenp1033 \ltrpar\qc {\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\cf2 [Box] }{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\cf4 What Steps Lead to Good Decisions?\par}\par\pard\plain\langnp1033\langfenp1033 \ltrpar\ql\fi-480\li480 {\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\cf6 1. }{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ab\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\cf6\b Ask Jehovah }{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\cf6 to help you decide what to do.\u8212?}{\field{\*\fldinst {HYPERLINK "https://www.jw.org/finder?pub=nwtsty&bible=59001005&wtlocale=E&srcid=share" }}{\fldrslt{\cs4\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\cf3\ul James 1:5}}}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\cf6 .\par}\pard\plain\langnp1033\langfenp1033 \ltrpar\ql\li720 {\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\cf2 [Image:]\u160?A woman praying.\par}\pard\plain\langnp1033\langfenp1033 \ltrpar\ql\fi-480\li480 {\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\cf6 2. }{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ab\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\cf6\b Do research }{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\cf6 in the Bible and Bible-based publications to find principles that apply. You may also consult experienced Christians.\par}\pard\plain\langnp1033\langfenp1033 \ltrpar\q